import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.CFT.MaxProP.ContCohomology.Defs

/-!
# The Frattini subgroup and Burnside's basis theorem for pro-`p` groups

For a pro-`p` group `G` the **Frattini subgroup**

`Φ(G) = closure(G^p · [G, G])`

is the intersection of the maximal open subgroups, and Burnside's basis theorem identifies the
topological generator rank with the first continuous cohomology:

`d(G) = dim_{𝔽_p} H¹_cont(G, 𝔽_p)`.

These are the pro-`p` group-theoretic facts behind the generator-rank preservation in
`Work.CFT.MaxProP.CuttingData` (`Submission/Work/CFT/MaxProP/Splitting.lean`).

## Main definitions

* `Work.CFT.MaxProP.proPFrattini p G` — the Frattini subgroup of a pro-`p` group.
* `Work.CFT.MaxProP.topGeneratorRank G` — the minimal number of topological generators.
-/

open NumberField
open scoped Classical nonZeroDivisors

noncomputable section

set_option maxHeartbeats 800000
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace Work.CFT.MaxProP

/-- The **Frattini subgroup of a pro-`p` group** `G`: the closed subgroup generated by the `p`-th
powers and the commutators.  For a pro-`p` group this is the intersection of the maximal open
subgroups, i.e. the kernel of the map to the maximal elementary abelian `p`-quotient. -/
def proPFrattini (p : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]
    [IsTopologicalGroup G] : Subgroup G :=
  (Subgroup.closure {x : G | ∃ a : G, x = a ^ p} ⊔
    Subgroup.closure {x : G | ∃ a b : G, x = a * b * a⁻¹ * b⁻¹}).topologicalClosure

/-- A profinite group `G` is a **pro-`p` group** if all its finite continuous quotients `G ⧸ U`
(over the open normal subgroups `U ◁ G`) are finite `p`-groups.

This is the correct notion for an *infinite* pro-`p` group: Mathlib's `IsPGroup p G` requires
every element of `G` to have `p`-power order, which fails for `ℤ_p` and for the maximal
everywhere-unramified pro-`p` group `G0 F p`. -/
def IsProPGroup (p : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] : Prop :=
  ∀ U : OpenNormal G, IsPGroup p (G ⧸ U.carrier)

/-- The **minimal number of topological generators** of a topological group `G`: the least `d`
such that the image of the free group on `d` generators is dense in `G`. -/
def topGeneratorRank (G : Type) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] : ℕ :=
  sInf {d : ℕ | ∃ f : FreeGroup (Fin d) →* G, closure (Set.range f) = Set.univ}

end Work.CFT.MaxProP
